{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833074181,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e463451b001YJ6UH0Z6HwnTGH","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","messageID":"msg_1e4632c80001mUVuU5ihpd39BT","type":"tool","id":"call_e3ce3476b2d74124afdb51a5","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review && grep -o '\"title\": \"[^\"]*\"' deep-review-findings-registry.json | sed 's/\"title\": //' | head -60"},"output":"\"--backfill executes the hook and the advisor CLI from the directory a run-log line names\"\n\"--backfill replays a started-command row with the default fixture path even when the run used a custom --fixture\"\n\"`make no changes to` reads a genuine no-edit request as a change request\"\n\"`make no changes` reads a scope-limiting change request as a no-edit request\"\n\"A --target-directory copy records the source as the file it changed\"\n\"A 2> or &> redirect target that names a command document still counts as a start\"\n\"A background & is folded into the writer's argument list\"\n\"A command that starts after a shell keyword or the command builtin is not read as a command start\"\n\"A coordinated refusal names the second command without a lead, so the typed path still delivers it\"\n\"A correction inside one document still attaches the creation workflow when the sentence carries a generic creation word\"\n\"A corrupt Devin sessions.db suppresses the transcript fallback\"\n\"A documented timeout consumer never reads the timeout variable\"\n\"A dotenv file tracked in the commit under test is cloned into the arena, because the dotenv guard runs only on the copied build trees\"\n\"A DSH operator message with no source object is silently reclassified as injected\"\n\"A failed write mid-apply leaves a half-embedded tree and prints no undo\"\n\"A file name git quotes cannot be restored, so one space in a created path stops the arm and leaves the file\"\n\"A fourth hand-spelled runtime list sits outside the parity test that exists to catch exactly this\"\n\"A heredoc whose delimiter is not a bare identifier is read as commands\"\n\"A listing above the cap is still reported as a spawn failure\"\n\"A long flag whose value is attached by shell quoting still reports ok for a command node refuses to run\"\n\"A measured turn inherits every credential the runner carries except the GitHub trio\"\n\"A mid-arm refusal names no row, so the stop cannot be tied to the log's last line\"\n\"A mode suffix hides a command reported twice\"\n\"A node argument node itself rejects still lets the next word read as the script\"\n\"A node flag with a space-separated value is read as the script word, so a working hook is reported missing\"\n\"A question or statement that names a doctor command with the noun command still passes that command row\"\n\"A question over an or-list still attaches its second command\"\n\"A refusal that quotes the COMMAND: format is scored as a start\"\n\"A refusal typed with the retired command name still delivers the live mutating command\"\n\"A second heredoc on one opening line is not stripped, so its body comparison becomes a write\"\n\"A separated value for a valid node flag is read as the hook script\"\n\"A shell read counts as a workflow load but not as a start or a loop\"\n\"A started-command row selected by --row-id is logged under the pre arm\"\n\"A symlinked .codex/AGENTS.md reports PASS while the manifest declares that path absent\"\n\"A symlinked REPO RULES.md or .cursor/rules/repo-local.md is written through, so apply mutates a file its plan never named\"\n\"A three-backtick line closes a four-backtick fence\"\n\"A write whose target is never named counts as inside the checkout, so a lookup plus an unnamed write scores as a readWrite start\"\n\"A10 counts report-only entries among the copies as expected\"\n\"A10 reports copies as expected for a tree whose CLAUDE.md is missing\"\n\"A11 malformed-row finding has no specific repair, while the A11 troubleshooting row points at a tool that cannot fix it\"\n\"An absent Codex advisor entry is routed to a command that cannot repair it and a promised repair line is never printed\"\n\"An arm named paired is silently hidden or overwritten by the summary pair block\"\n\"An attached node evaluation flag still reports the hook as wired\"\n\"An or-list refusal that names its second command as \\\"\n\"An or-list whose non-final item is a two-word /doctor command still publishes the refused command\"\n\"Automatic rollback restores the backup without the allowlist and hash checks the manual restore enforces\"\n\"Capping stderr at 1 MiB hides a SQLITE_BUSY marker written past the cap, so the busy retry no longer fires\"\n\"CLI disable loop filters out every MK_ alias, so the direct-call path never exercises those names\"\n\"Codex opens the caller's locator after containment resolved a different path\"\n\"COMMAND_POLICIES is generated, drift-guarded and documented as the attach-path policy lookup, but no code reads it\"\n\"Containment is inferred from no git remote with no assertion that the checkout is a prepared arena\"\n\"Containment is proven on the resolved path while the bytes are opened from the caller path\"\n\"CP-003 control call can abstain under a switch alias it never unsets\"\n\"Dead empty conditional in primaryIntentBonus\"\n\"Deep-loop depth gate is satisfied by any typed /deep: prefix, not the attached command\"\n\"Five line citations in advisor-recommend.md point at unrelated code\"\n\"Gate assertion passes a table without the requested mode\"\n\"Generated leaf manifest skips the DSH hook README while listing its three siblings\"\n\"Hook wiring counts a marker anywhere in the event payload so a mention is read as a wired entry\"\n\"Hub-attached commands skip the no-edit gate the command scorer applies\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"--backfill executes the hook and the advisor CLI from the directory a run-log line names\"\n\"--backfill replays a started-command row with the default fixture path even when the run used a custom --fixture\"\n\"`make no changes to` reads a genuine no-edit request as a change request\"\n\"`make no changes` reads a scope-limiting change request as a no-edit request\"\n\"A --target-directory copy records the source as the file it changed\"\n\"A 2> or &> redirect target that names a command document still counts as a start\"\n\"A background & is folded into the writer's argument list\"\n\"A command that starts after a shell keyword or the command builtin is not read as a command start\"\n\"A coordinated refusal names the second command without a lead, so the typed path still delivers it\"\n\"A correction inside one document still attaches the creation workflow when the sentence carries a generic creation word\"\n\"A corrupt Devin sessions.db suppresses the transcript fallback\"\n\"A documented timeout consumer never reads the timeout variable\"\n\"A dotenv file tracked in the commit under test is cloned into the arena, because the dotenv guard runs only on the copied build trees\"\n\"A DSH operator message with no source object is silently reclassified as injected\"\n\"A failed write mid-apply leaves a half-embedded tree and prints no undo\"\n\"A file name git quotes cannot be restored, so one space in a created path stops the arm and leaves the file\"\n\"A fourth hand-spelled runtime list sits outside the parity test that exists to catch exactly this\"\n\"A heredoc whose delimiter is not a bare identifier is read as commands\"\n\"A listing above the cap is still reported as a spawn failure\"\n\"A long flag whose value is attached by shell quoting still reports ok for a command node refuses to run\"\n\"A measured turn inherits every credential the runner carries except the GitHub trio\"\n\"A mid-arm refusal names no row, so the stop cannot be tied to the log's last line\"\n\"A mode suffix hides a command reported twice\"\n\"A node argument node itself rejects still lets the next word read as the script\"\n\"A node flag with a space-separated value is read as the script word, so a working hook is reported missing\"\n\"A question or statement that names a doctor command with the noun command still passes that command row\"\n\"A question over an or-list still attaches its second command\"\n\"A refusal that quotes the COMMAND: format is scored as a start\"\n\"A refusal typed with the retired command name still delivers the live mutating command\"\n\"A second heredoc on one opening line is not stripped, so its body comparison becomes a write\"\n\"A separated value for a valid node flag is read as the hook script\"\n\"A shell read counts as a workflow load but not as a start or a loop\"\n\"A started-command row selected by --row-id is logged under the pre arm\"\n\"A symlinked .codex/AGENTS.md reports PASS while the manifest declares that path absent\"\n\"A symlinked REPO RULES.md or .cursor/rules/repo-local.md is written through, so apply mutates a file its plan never named\"\n\"A three-backtick line closes a four-backtick fence\"\n\"A write whose target is never named counts as inside the checkout, so a lookup plus an unnamed write scores as a readWrite start\"\n\"A10 counts report-only entries among the copies as expected\"\n\"A10 reports copies as expected for a tree whose CLAUDE.md is missing\"\n\"A11 malformed-row finding has no specific repair, while the A11 troubleshooting row points at a tool that cannot fix it\"\n\"An absent Codex advisor entry is routed to a command that cannot repair it and a promised repair line is never printed\"\n\"An arm named paired is silently hidden or overwritten by the summary pair block\"\n\"An attached node evaluation flag still reports the hook as wired\"\n\"An or-list refusal that names its second command as \\\"\n\"An or-list whose non-final item is a two-word /doctor command still publishes the refused command\"\n\"Automatic rollback restores the backup without the allowlist and hash checks the manual restore enforces\"\n\"Capping stderr at 1 MiB hides a SQLITE_BUSY marker written past the cap, so the busy retry no longer fires\"\n\"CLI disable loop filters out every MK_ alias, so the direct-call path never exercises those names\"\n\"Codex opens the caller's locator after containment resolved a different path\"\n\"COMMAND_POLICIES is generated, drift-guarded and documented as the attach-path policy lookup, but no code reads it\"\n\"Containment is inferred from no git remote with no assertion that the checkout is a prepared arena\"\n\"Containment is proven on the resolved path while the bytes are opened from the caller path\"\n\"CP-003 control call can abstain under a switch alias it never unsets\"\n\"Dead empty conditional in primaryIntentBonus\"\n\"Deep-loop depth gate is satisfied by any typed /deep: prefix, not the attached command\"\n\"Five line citations in advisor-recommend.md point at unrelated code\"\n\"Gate assertion passes a table without the requested mode\"\n\"Generated leaf manifest skips the DSH hook README while listing its three siblings\"\n\"Hook wiring counts a marker anywhere in the event payload so a mention is read as a wired entry\"\n\"Hub-attached commands skip the no-edit gate the command scorer applies\"\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review && grep -o '\\\"title\\\": \\\"[^\\\"]*\\\"' deep-review-findings-registry.json | sed 's/\\\"title\\\": //' | head -60\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833073435,"end":1794833074181}}}}
