{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794833513323,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","part":{"id":"prt_1e469fb6b001MekS66ya52Hgxq","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","messageID":"msg_1e469f5ad001bysD7tymqA92A3","type":"step-start","snapshot":"db967df823979e4548e12f02210470b7ac8f089d"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833514353,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e469fb6d001kLi0izZJA5qLaq","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","messageID":"msg_1e469f5ad001bysD7tymqA92A3","type":"tool","id":"call_2db3057d0fe24d67921fbadd","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '58,140p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs; echo \"=== main ===\"; sed -n '430,533p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs"},"output":"function parseArgs(argv = process.argv.slice(2)) {\n  const knownFlags = ['mode', 'runDirectory', 'runDir', 'specFolder', 'eventJson', 'eventJsonPath', 'policyId'];\n  const args = {};\n  for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i += 1) {\n    const token = argv[i];\n    if (!token.startsWith('--')) {\n      throw new Error(`Unexpected positional argument: ${token}`);\n    }\n    const key = token.slice(2).replace(/-([a-z])/g, (_, c) => c.toUpperCase());\n    if (!knownFlags.includes(key)) {\n      const error = new Error(`Unknown option: --${token.slice(2)}`);\n      error.code = 'INPUT_VALIDATION';\n      throw error;\n    }\n    const next = argv[i + 1];\n    if (next === undefined || next.startsWith('--')) {\n      args[key] = true;\n    } else {\n      args[key] = next;\n      i += 1;\n    }\n  }\n  return args;\n}\n\nfunction requireString(args, ...keys) {\n  for (const key of keys) {\n    if (args[key] && typeof args[key] === 'string') {\n      return args[key];\n    }\n  }\n  throw new Error(`${keys[0]} is required`);\n}\n\n// Key order carries no meaning in an event the caller hands over, so the\n// digest sorts keys before hashing.\nfunction stableJson(value) {\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) return `[${value.map(stableJson).join(',')}]`;\n  if (value !== null && typeof value === 'object') {\n    return `{${Object.keys(value).sort()\n      .map((key) => `${JSON.stringify(key)}:${stableJson(value[key])}`)\n      .join(',')}}`;\n  }\n  return JSON.stringify(value);\n}\n\nfunction jsonOut(payload) {\n  process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(payload)}\\n`);\n}\n\nfunction normalizeMode(mode) {\n  if (!mode || typeof mode !== 'string') return '';\n  const trimmed = mode.trim();\n  if (trimmed === 'research' || trimmed === 'deep-research') return 'deep-research';\n  if (trimmed === 'review' || trimmed === 'deep-review') return 'deep-review';\n  return trimmed;\n}\n\nasync function resolveModeAdapter(mode) {\n  const normalized = normalizeMode(mode);\n  switch (normalized) {\n    case 'deep-research': {\n      const mod = await import('../lib/deep-research-ledger-schema/index.ts');\n      return {\n        normalizedMode: 'deep-research',\n        createRegistry: mod.createDeepResearchEventRegistry,\n        prepareEvent: mod.prepareDeepResearchEvent,\n        isEventStem: mod.isDeepResearchEventStem,\n      };\n    }\n    case 'deep-review': {\n      const mod = await import('../lib/deep-review-ledger-schema/index.ts');\n      return {\n        normalizedMode: 'deep-review',\n        createRegistry: mod.createDeepReviewEventRegistry,\n        prepareEvent: mod.prepareDeepReviewEvent,\n        isEventStem: mod.isDeepReviewEventStem,\n      };\n    }\n    default:\n      throw new Error(`Unsupported mode: ${mode}`);\n  }\n}\n=== main ===\n    && rawEvent\n    && typeof rawEvent === 'object'\n    && !Array.isArray(rawEvent)\n    && (rawEvent.type === 'iteration' || rawEvent.type === 'iteration_start'\n      || (rawEvent.type === 'event'\n        && [\n          'dispatch_failure',\n          'dispatch_receipt_write_failed',\n          'verification_degraded',\n          'containment_violation',\n          'containment_contested',\n        ].includes(rawEvent.event)))\n  ) {\n    // The review agent, its iteration prompt and its workflow all hand the gateway the canonical\n    // iteration record itself, the pre-dispatch executor audit hands it the iteration's opening\n    // row, the audited executor runner hands it a dispatch's failure rows, the post-dispatch\n    // validator its verification_degraded row and the write-containment guard its findings.\n    // Their optional fields vary with review depth and executor, so each travels whole under one\n    // stem, and the state projection writes it back as the same row.\n    const sessionId = typeof rawEvent.sessionId === 'string' && rawEvent.sessionId\n      ? rawEvent.sessionId\n      : 'run-cli';\n    const preparedInput = buildPreparedInput({\n      stem: 'deep_review.iteration_recorded',\n      scope: { runId: sessionId, sessionId },\n      data: { record: rawEvent },\n      prevEventHash: currentHead.recordHash,\n      replay: defaultReplay,\n    }, rawEvent);\n    eventRecord = adapter.prepareEvent(preparedInput, registry);\n  } else {\n    throw new Error('Unrecognized event format: expected object with stem or event_type');\n  }\n\n  const outcome = await appendModeEvent({\n    mode: normalizedMode,\n    runDirectory,\n    eventRecord,\n    authorityRoot,\n    policy: {\n      policyId: resolvedPolicy.policyId,\n      policyVersion: resolvedPolicy.policyVersion,\n      policyDigest: resolvedPolicy.digest,\n    },\n    policyRegistry,\n    authorizationGateway,\n    ledger,\n    eventRegistry: registry,\n    binding,\n  });\n\n  // Both phases leave the state log out of step with the ledger, so the runner\n  // reads either one back to name why a lineage recorded nothing.\n  if (outcome && outcome.ok === false && (outcome.phase === 'projection' || outcome.phase === 'provenance')) {\n    const eventStem = eventRecord?.envelope?.payload?.stem;\n    const refusalRecord = {\n      at: new Date().toISOString(),\n      mode: normalizedMode,\n      phase: outcome.phase,\n      code: outcome.code,\n      reason: outcome.reason,\n      ...(typeof eventStem === 'string' && eventStem ? { stem: eventStem } : {}),\n    };\n    try {\n      fs.appendFileSync(\n        path.join(runDirectory, 'gateway-refusals.jsonl'),\n        `${JSON.stringify(refusalRecord)}\\n`,\n        'utf8',\n      );\n    } catch {\n      // The refusal record is best-effort and must not change the CLI result.\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Surface a lossy legacy migration instead of letting it pass silently. Only\n  // the legacy upcast path sets legacyWarnings, so canonical/stem/event_type\n  // outputs stay byte-identical to before.\n  if (legacyWarnings && legacyWarnings.length > 0) {\n    jsonOut({ ...outcome, warnings: [...legacyWarnings] });\n  } else {\n    jsonOut(outcome);\n  }\n  process.exit(outcome.ok ? 0 : 2);\n}\n\nif (require.main === module && isTsxLoaded) {\n  main().catch((error) => {\n    jsonOut({\n      ok: false,\n      phase: 'runtime',\n      reason: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n      code: error && error.code === 'INPUT_VALIDATION' ? 'INPUT_VALIDATION' : 'RUNTIME_ERROR',\n    });\n    process.exit(error && error.code === 'INPUT_VALIDATION' ? 3 : 1);\n  });\n}\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  stableJson,\n  parseArgs,\n  normalizeMode,\n  resolveModeAdapter,\n  main,\n};\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"function parseArgs(argv = process.argv.slice(2)) {\n  const knownFlags = ['mode', 'runDirectory', 'runDir', 'specFolder', 'eventJson', 'eventJsonPath', 'policyId'];\n  const args = {};\n  for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i += 1) {\n    const token = argv[i];\n    if (!token.startsWith('--')) {\n      throw new Error(`Unexpected positional argument: ${token}`);\n    }\n    const key = token.slice(2).replace(/-([a-z])/g, (_, c) => c.toUpperCase());\n    if (!knownFlags.includes(key)) {\n      const error = new Error(`Unknown option: --${token.slice(2)}`);\n      error.code = 'INPUT_VALIDATION';\n      throw error;\n    }\n    const next = argv[i + 1];\n    if (next === undefined || next.startsWith('--')) {\n      args[key] = true;\n    } else {\n      args[key] = next;\n      i += 1;\n    }\n  }\n  return args;\n}\n\nfunction requireString(args, ...keys) {\n  for (const key of keys) {\n    if (args[key] && typeof args[key] === 'string') {\n      return args[key];\n    }\n  }\n  throw new Error(`${keys[0]} is required`);\n}\n\n// Key order carries no meaning in an event the caller hands over, so the\n// digest sorts keys before hashing.\nfunction stableJson(value) {\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) return `[${value.map(stableJson).join(',')}]`;\n  if (value !== null && typeof value === 'object') {\n    return `{${Object.keys(value).sort()\n      .map((key) => `${JSON.stringify(key)}:${stableJson(value[key])}`)\n      .join(',')}}`;\n  }\n  return JSON.stringify(value);\n}\n\nfunction jsonOut(payload) {\n  process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(payload)}\\n`);\n}\n\nfunction normalizeMode(mode) {\n  if (!mode || typeof mode !== 'string') return '';\n  const trimmed = mode.trim();\n  if (trimmed === 'research' || trimmed === 'deep-research') return 'deep-research';\n  if (trimmed === 'review' || trimmed === 'deep-review') return 'deep-review';\n  return trimmed;\n}\n\nasync function resolveModeAdapter(mode) {\n  const normalized = normalizeMode(mode);\n  switch (normalized) {\n    case 'deep-research': {\n      const mod = await import('../lib/deep-research-ledger-schema/index.ts');\n      return {\n        normalizedMode: 'deep-research',\n        createRegistry: mod.createDeepResearchEventRegistry,\n        prepareEvent: mod.prepareDeepResearchEvent,\n        isEventStem: mod.isDeepResearchEventStem,\n      };\n    }\n    case 'deep-review': {\n      const mod = await import('../lib/deep-review-ledger-schema/index.ts');\n      return {\n        normalizedMode: 'deep-review',\n        createRegistry: mod.createDeepReviewEventRegistry,\n        prepareEvent: mod.prepareDeepReviewEvent,\n        isEventStem: mod.isDeepReviewEventStem,\n      };\n    }\n    default:\n      throw new Error(`Unsupported mode: ${mode}`);\n  }\n}\n=== main ===\n    && rawEvent\n    && typeof rawEvent === 'object'\n    && !Array.isArray(rawEvent)\n    && (rawEvent.type === 'iteration' || rawEvent.type === 'iteration_start'\n      || (rawEvent.type === 'event'\n        && [\n          'dispatch_failure',\n          'dispatch_receipt_write_failed',\n          'verification_degraded',\n          'containment_violation',\n          'containment_contested',\n        ].includes(rawEvent.event)))\n  ) {\n    // The review agent, its iteration prompt and its workflow all hand the gateway the canonical\n    // iteration record itself, the pre-dispatch executor audit hands it the iteration's opening\n    // row, the audited executor runner hands it a dispatch's failure rows, the post-dispatch\n    // validator its verification_degraded row and the write-containment guard its findings.\n    // Their optional fields vary with review depth and executor, so each travels whole under one\n    // stem, and the state projection writes it back as the same row.\n    const sessionId = typeof rawEvent.sessionId === 'string' && rawEvent.sessionId\n      ? rawEvent.sessionId\n      : 'run-cli';\n    const preparedInput = buildPreparedInput({\n      stem: 'deep_review.iteration_recorded',\n      scope: { runId: sessionId, sessionId },\n      data: { record: rawEvent },\n      prevEventHash: currentHead.recordHash,\n      replay: defaultReplay,\n    }, rawEvent);\n    eventRecord = adapter.prepareEvent(preparedInput, registry);\n  } else {\n    throw new Error('Unrecognized event format: expected object with stem or event_type');\n  }\n\n  const outcome = await appendModeEvent({\n    mode: normalizedMode,\n    runDirectory,\n    eventRecord,\n    authorityRoot,\n    policy: {\n      policyId: resolvedPolicy.policyId,\n      policyVersion: resolvedPolicy.policyVersion,\n      policyDigest: resolvedPolicy.digest,\n    },\n    policyRegistry,\n    authorizationGateway,\n    ledger,\n    eventRegistry: registry,\n    binding,\n  });\n\n  // Both phases leave the state log out of step with the ledger, so the runner\n  // reads either one back to name why a lineage recorded nothing.\n  if (outcome && outcome.ok === false && (outcome.phase === 'projection' || outcome.phase === 'provenance')) {\n    const eventStem = eventRecord?.envelope?.payload?.stem;\n    const refusalRecord = {\n      at: new Date().toISOString(),\n      mode: normalizedMode,\n      phase: outcome.phase,\n      code: outcome.code,\n      reason: outcome.reason,\n      ...(typeof eventStem === 'string' && eventStem ? { stem: eventStem } : {}),\n    };\n    try {\n      fs.appendFileSync(\n        path.join(runDirectory, 'gateway-refusals.jsonl'),\n        `${JSON.stringify(refusalRecord)}\\n`,\n        'utf8',\n      );\n    } catch {\n      // The refusal record is best-effort and must not change the CLI result.\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Surface a lossy legacy migration instead of letting it pass silently. Only\n  // the legacy upcast path sets legacyWarnings, so canonical/stem/event_type\n  // outputs stay byte-identical to before.\n  if (legacyWarnings && legacyWarnings.length > 0) {\n    jsonOut({ ...outcome, warnings: [...legacyWarnings] });\n  } else {\n    jsonOut(outcome);\n  }\n  process.exit(outcome.ok ? 0 : 2);\n}\n\nif (require.main === module && isTsxLoaded) {\n  main().catch((error) => {\n    jsonOut({\n      ok: false,\n      phase: 'runtime',\n      reason: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n      code: error && error.code === 'INPUT_VALIDATION' ? 'INPUT_VALIDATION' : 'RUNTIME_ERROR',\n    });\n    process.exit(error && error.code === 'INPUT_VALIDATION' ? 3 : 1);\n  });\n}\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  stableJson,\n  parseArgs,\n  normalizeMode,\n  resolveModeAdapter,\n  main,\n};\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '58,140p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs; echo \\\"=== main ===\\\"; sed -n '430,533p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833513325,"end":1794833514353}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794833515518,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","part":{"id":"prt_1e46a03fe001mHJSXf0MfsH4Sk","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","messageID":"msg_1e469f5ad001bysD7tymqA92A3","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"db967df823979e4548e12f02210470b7ac8f089d","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":530,"output":126,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":131840,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794833518008,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","part":{"id":"prt_1e46a0db8001I1aJ7opZ3Q6dpn","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","messageID":"msg_1e46a0404001t08sCkOHF2Bbsf","type":"step-start","snapshot":"db967df823979e4548e12f02210470b7ac8f089d"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833519961,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e46a1278001dL7HoX0hB9U30H","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","messageID":"msg_1e46a0404001t08sCkOHF2Bbsf","type":"tool","id":"call_6584aede32ea4cbabcc547b2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '720,800p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"      step_create_state_log:\n        action: \"Open the run in the ledger: record deep_review.run_initialized through the append gateway, which writes the state log's first row\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        note: |\n          The state log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger, so this step never writes\n          it directly. A config row written beside the ledger carries keys the projection cannot\n          rebuild, and the projection refuses to drop them, so every later append in the run would\n          commit to the ledger and then exit 2. Recording the run's opening as a ledger event makes\n          the projected config row the state log's first row from the start. The full config stays\n          in deep-review-config.json, which is what the reducer reads.\n        command: |\n          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n          node -e '\n            const fs = require(\"fs\"), crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n            const [configPath, workflowPath] = process.argv.slice(1);\n            const sha = (bytes) => crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(bytes).digest(\"hex\");\n            const raw = fs.readFileSync(configPath);\n            const config = JSON.parse(raw);\n            const targetTypes = { files: \"file\", file: \"file\", directory: \"directory\", \"spec-folder\": \"directory\", track: \"directory\", repository: \"repository\" };\n            const lineageModes = { new: \"fresh\", fresh: \"fresh\", restart: \"restart\", resume: \"resume\" };\n            // The projected config row shows this topic; one the schema cannot hold is left out,\n            // and the row falls back to the run id rather than the run failing to open.\n            const topic = typeof config.topic === \"string\" && config.topic.trim() !== \"\" && config.topic.length <= 4096\n              ? config.topic\n              : null;\n            process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({\n              stem: \"deep_review.run_initialized\",\n              scope: { runId: config.sessionId, sessionId: config.sessionId, generation: Number(config.generation) || 1 },\n              data: {\n                target: {\n                  targetId: \"review-target\",\n                  targetType: targetTypes[config.reviewTargetType] || \"artifact\",\n                  artifactRef: \"deep-review-config.json#reviewTarget\",\n                  sourceDigest: sha(String(config.reviewTarget)),\n                  contentDigest: sha(raw),\n                },\n                lineageMode: lineageModes[config.lineageMode] || \"fresh\",\n                maxIterations: Number(config.maxIterations),\n                convergencePolicyVersion: \"convergence-policy@\" + ((config.antiConvergence && config.antiConvergence.convergenceMode) || \"default\"),\n                reviewModeContractDigest: sha(fs.readFileSync(workflowPath)),\n                initialReleaseReadinessState: \"not-assessed\",\n                ...(topic === null ? {} : { topic }),\n              },\n            }));\n          ' \"{state_paths.config}\" \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n          node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n          STATUS=$?\n          rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n          exit \"$STATUS\"\n        output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n\n      step_record_restarted_run:\n        skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n        action: \"Record the restarted lineage after the run-open row so the restart marker never precedes deep_review.run_initialized\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n\n      step_create_findings_registry:\n        action: \"Initialize reducer-owned review findings registry\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        content: '{\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"generation\":{generation_init},\"lineageMode\":\"{lineage_mode_init}\",\"openFindings\":[],\"resolvedFindings\":[],\"repeatedFindings\":[],\"dimensionCoverage\":{\"correctness\":false,\"security\":false,\"traceability\":false,\"maintainability\":false},\"findingsBySeverity\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"openFindingsCount\":0,\"resolvedFindingsCount\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0.0}'\n        output: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n\n      step_create_strategy:\n        action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n        populate:\n          review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n          review_target_type: \"{review_target_type}\"\n          dimensions: \"{dimension_queue}\"\n          scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n          cross_reference_targets: \"{cross_reference_targets}\"\n          max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n          convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n          stop_policy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n        output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n\n      step_seed_coverage_graph:\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"      step_create_state_log:\n        action: \"Open the run in the ledger: record deep_review.run_initialized through the append gateway, which writes the state log's first row\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        note: |\n          The state log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger, so this step never writes\n          it directly. A config row written beside the ledger carries keys the projection cannot\n          rebuild, and the projection refuses to drop them, so every later append in the run would\n          commit to the ledger and then exit 2. Recording the run's opening as a ledger event makes\n          the projected config row the state log's first row from the start. The full config stays\n          in deep-review-config.json, which is what the reducer reads.\n        command: |\n          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n          node -e '\n            const fs = require(\"fs\"), crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n            const [configPath, workflowPath] = process.argv.slice(1);\n            const sha = (bytes) => crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(bytes).digest(\"hex\");\n            const raw = fs.readFileSync(configPath);\n            const config = JSON.parse(raw);\n            const targetTypes = { files: \"file\", file: \"file\", directory: \"directory\", \"spec-folder\": \"directory\", track: \"directory\", repository: \"repository\" };\n            const lineageModes = { new: \"fresh\", fresh: \"fresh\", restart: \"restart\", resume: \"resume\" };\n            // The projected config row shows this topic; one the schema cannot hold is left out,\n            // and the row falls back to the run id rather than the run failing to open.\n            const topic = typeof config.topic === \"string\" && config.topic.trim() !== \"\" && config.topic.length <= 4096\n              ? config.topic\n              : null;\n            process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({\n              stem: \"deep_review.run_initialized\",\n              scope: { runId: config.sessionId, sessionId: config.sessionId, generation: Number(config.generation) || 1 },\n              data: {\n                target: {\n                  targetId: \"review-target\",\n                  targetType: targetTypes[config.reviewTargetType] || \"artifact\",\n                  artifactRef: \"deep-review-config.json#reviewTarget\",\n                  sourceDigest: sha(String(config.reviewTarget)),\n                  contentDigest: sha(raw),\n                },\n                lineageMode: lineageModes[config.lineageMode] || \"fresh\",\n                maxIterations: Number(config.maxIterations),\n                convergencePolicyVersion: \"convergence-policy@\" + ((config.antiConvergence && config.antiConvergence.convergenceMode) || \"default\"),\n                reviewModeContractDigest: sha(fs.readFileSync(workflowPath)),\n                initialReleaseReadinessState: \"not-assessed\",\n                ...(topic === null ? {} : { topic }),\n              },\n            }));\n          ' \"{state_paths.config}\" \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n          node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n          STATUS=$?\n          rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n          exit \"$STATUS\"\n        output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n\n      step_record_restarted_run:\n        skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n        action: \"Record the restarted lineage after the run-open row so the restart marker never precedes deep_review.run_initialized\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n\n      step_create_findings_registry:\n        action: \"Initialize reducer-owned review findings registry\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        content: '{\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"generation\":{generation_init},\"lineageMode\":\"{lineage_mode_init}\",\"openFindings\":[],\"resolvedFindings\":[],\"repeatedFindings\":[],\"dimensionCoverage\":{\"correctness\":false,\"security\":false,\"traceability\":false,\"maintainability\":false},\"findingsBySeverity\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"openFindingsCount\":0,\"resolvedFindingsCount\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0.0}'\n        output: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n\n      step_create_strategy:\n        action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n        populate:\n          review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n          review_target_type: \"{review_target_type}\"\n          dimensions: \"{dimension_queue}\"\n          scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n          cross_reference_targets: \"{cross_reference_targets}\"\n          max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n          convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n          stop_policy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n        output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n\n      step_seed_coverage_graph:\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '720,800p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833519224,"end":1794833519961}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794833521055,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","part":{"id":"prt_1e46a199f001RltFr3mTvuYxev","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","messageID":"msg_1e46a0404001t08sCkOHF2Bbsf","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"db967df823979e4548e12f02210470b7ac8f089d","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1760,"output":81,"reasoning":78,"cache":{"read":132352,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794833523473,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","part":{"id":"prt_1e46a2311001rtxXBNYnelG5Mt","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","messageID":"msg_1e46a19a4001zyT0305VAt0Fr9","type":"step-start","snapshot":"db967df823979e4548e12f02210470b7ac8f089d"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833528229,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e46a30d80011m7Ovg1wL3k8am","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","messageID":"msg_1e46a19a4001zyT0305VAt0Fr9","type":"tool","id":"call_ea3d26d6ca744acd8c1c3a2a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-218\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to review/ during initialization to track review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review strategy template\"\n6:   - \"review dimension tracking\"\n7:   - \"exhausted review approaches\"\n8:   - \"review session tracking\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: planning\n11: version: 1.11.0.13\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n15: \n16: Runtime template copied into the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` during initialization. Tracks review progress across iterations.\n17: \n18: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n19: \n20: ### Purpose\n21: \n22: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep review session. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n23: \n24: ### Usage\n25: \n26: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Review Dimensions, Known Context, and Review Boundaries from config and memory context.\n27: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned dimension/files, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n28: - **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n29: - **Protection:** None (shared mutable state). Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n30: - **Ownership:** Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 2. TOPIC\n35: [Review target description from config -- set during initialization]\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n40: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n41: - [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n42: - [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n43: - [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n44: - [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n45: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n46: \n47: ---\n48: \n49: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n50: [What this review session is NOT trying to assess -- populated during initialization]\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n55: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n60: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n61: [None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n62: \n63: | Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n64: |-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n65: | [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\n66: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n71: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n72: - **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n73: - **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n74: - **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n75: - **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n76: \n77: [Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n78: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n83: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n84: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n89: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n90: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n95: [Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n96: \n97: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n98: - What was tried: [specific review approaches attempted]\n99: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n100: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n101: \n102: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n103: - What worked: [successful review approaches in this category]\n104: - Prefer for: [related dimensions where this category may help]\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n109: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n110: - Completed pivots: 0\n111: - Failed pivots: 0\n112: - Audited overrides: 0\n113: - Swept: none yet\n114: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n115: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n116: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n117: \n118: ---\n119: \n120: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n121: [Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n122: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n123: \n124: ---\n125: \n126: ## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n127: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n128: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration. Includes target dimension and/or specific files to review.]\n129: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n134: [Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n135: \n136: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n137: \n138: Populate during initialization before the first review dimension runs. Keep this pointer-based and scoped to the declared review target:\n139: \n140: - Target pointers: files, specs, symbols, or resource-map entries under review.\n141: - Behavior claims: acceptance criteria, public contracts, or docs to verify.\n142: - Reuse and conventions: existing patterns that define expected implementation shape.\n143: - Review risks and gaps: stale graph or memory caveats, missing files, and out-of-scope areas.\n144: \n145: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use this snapshot only to seed review dimensions and final traceability.\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n150: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n151: [Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n152: \n153: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n154: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n155: | `spec_code` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n156: | `checklist_evidence` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n157: | `skill_agent` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n158: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n159: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n160: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n161: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n162: \n163: ---\n164: \n165: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n166: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n167: [Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\n168: \n169: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n170: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n171: | [path/to/file] | [D1, D3] | [N] | [0 P0, 1 P1, 2 P2] | [partial/complete] |\n172: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n173: \n174: ---\n175: \n176: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n177: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n178: - Max iterations: [from config]\n179: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n180: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n181: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n182: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n183: - Session lineage: sessionId=[from config.sessionId], parentSessionId=[from config.parentSessionId], generation=[from config.generation], lineageMode=[from config.lineageMode]\n184: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n185: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n186: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n187: - Severity threshold: [from config.severityThreshold]\n188: - Review target type: [from config.reviewTargetType]\n189: - Cross-reference checks: core=[from config.crossReference.core], overlay=[from config.crossReference.overlay]\n190: - Started: [timestamp]\n191: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n192: \n193: ---\n194: \n195: ## 17. EXAMPLE (POPULATED)\n196: \n197: Reference snippet showing a partially populated strategy file mid-review. Use this as a visual anchor when opening a live strategy doc.\n198: \n199: ```markdown\n200: ## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n201: - Target: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research (skill, v1.4.0)\n202: - Dimensions: correctness, test-coverage, cross-runtime-parity, observability\n203: - Stop conditions: rolling newInfoRatio < 0.08 for 2 iterations OR all dimensions converged OR max=7 reached\n204: - Success criteria: zero P0 in correctness; test-coverage P0 resolved or deferred with rationale\n205: \n206: ## 4. NEXT FOCUS\n207: - Dimension: test-coverage\n208: - Files: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/deep-research-contract-parity.vitest.ts\n209: - Why: Iteration 2 surfaced a P0 (convergence-path coverage gap); needs a focused follow-up before correctness can terminate PASS.\n210: \n211: ## 9. COVERAGE MATRIX\n212: | Dimension            | Status     | Iterations touched |\n213: |----------------------|------------|--------------------|\n214: | correctness          | converged  | 1                  |\n215: | test-coverage        | converging | 2, 4               |\n216: | cross-runtime-parity | converging | 3                  |\n217: | observability        | converging | 4                  |\n218: ```","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-218\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to review/ during initialization to track review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review strategy template\"\n6:   - \"review dimension tracking\"\n7:   - \"exhausted review approaches\"\n8:   - \"review session tracking\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: planning\n11: version: 1.11.0.13\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n15: \n16: Runtime template copied into the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` during initialization. Tracks review progress across iterations.\n17: \n18: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n19: \n20: ### Purpose\n21: \n22: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep review session. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n23: \n24: ### Usage\n25: \n26: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Review Dimensions, Known Context, and Review Boundaries from config and memory context.\n27: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned dimension/files, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n28: - **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n29: - **Protection:** None (shared mutable state). Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n30: - **Ownership:** Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 2. TOPIC\n35: [Review target description from config -- set during initialization]\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n40: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n41: - [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n42: - [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n43: - [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n44: - [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n45: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n46: \n47: ---\n48: \n49: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n50: [What this review session is NOT trying to assess -- populated during initialization]\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n55: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n60: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n61: [None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n62: \n63: | Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n64: |-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n65: | [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\n66: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n71: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n72: - **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n73: - **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n74: - **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n75: - **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n76: \n77: [Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n78: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n83: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n84: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n89: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n90: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n95: [Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n96: \n97: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n98: - What was tried: [specific review approaches attempted]\n99: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n100: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n101: \n102: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n103: - What worked: [successful review approaches in this category]\n104: - Prefer for: [related dimensions where this category may help]\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n109: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n110: - Completed pivots: 0\n111: - Failed pivots: 0\n112: - Audited overrides: 0\n113: - Swept: none yet\n114: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n115: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n116: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n117: \n118: ---\n119: \n120: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n121: [Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n122: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n123: \n124: ---\n125: \n126: ## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n127: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n128: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration. Includes target dimension and/or specific files to review.]\n129: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n134: [Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n135: \n136: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n137: \n138: Populate during initialization before the first review dimension runs. Keep this pointer-based and scoped to the declared review target:\n139: \n140: - Target pointers: files, specs, symbols, or resource-map entries under review.\n141: - Behavior claims: acceptance criteria, public contracts, or docs to verify.\n142: - Reuse and conventions: existing patterns that define expected implementation shape.\n143: - Review risks and gaps: stale graph or memory caveats, missing files, and out-of-scope areas.\n144: \n145: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use this snapshot only to seed review dimensions and final traceability.\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n150: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n151: [Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n152: \n153: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n154: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n155: | `spec_code` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n156: | `checklist_evidence` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n157: | `skill_agent` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n158: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n159: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n160: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n161: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n162: \n163: ---\n164: \n165: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n166: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n167: [Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\n168: \n169: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n170: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n171: | [path/to/file] | [D1, D3] | [N] | [0 P0, 1 P1, 2 P2] | [partial/complete] |\n172: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n173: \n174: ---\n175: \n176: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n177: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n178: - Max iterations: [from config]\n179: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n180: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n181: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n182: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n183: - Session lineage: sessionId=[from config.sessionId], parentSessionId=[from config.parentSessionId], generation=[from config.generation], lineageMode=[from config.lineageMode]\n184: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n185: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n186: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n187: - Severity threshold: [from config.severityThreshold]\n188: - Review target type: [from config.reviewTargetType]\n189: - Cross-reference checks: core=[from config.crossReference.core], overlay=[from config.crossReference.overlay]\n190: - Started: [timestamp]\n191: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n192: \n193: ---\n194: \n195: ## 17. EXAMPLE (POPULATED)\n196: \n197: Reference snippet showing a partially populated strategy file mid-review. Use this as a visual anchor when opening a live strategy doc.\n198: \n199: ```markdown\n200: ## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n201: - Target: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research (skill, v1.4.0)\n202: - Dimensions: correctness, test-coverage, cross-runtime-parity, observability\n203: - Stop conditions: rolling newInfoRatio < 0.08 for 2 iterations OR all dimensions converged OR max=7 reached\n204: - Success criteria: zero P0 in correctness; test-coverage P0 resolved or deferred with rationale\n205: \n206: ## 4. NEXT FOCUS\n207: - Dimension: test-coverage\n208: - Files: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/deep-research-contract-parity.vitest.ts\n209: - Why: Iteration 2 surfaced a P0 (convergence-path coverage gap); needs a focused follow-up before correctness can terminate PASS.\n210: \n211: ## 9. COVERAGE MATRIX\n212: | Dimension            | Status     | Iterations touched |\n213: |----------------------|------------|--------------------|\n214: | correctness          | converged  | 1                  |\n215: | test-coverage        | converging | 2, 4               |\n216: | cross-runtime-parity | converging | 3                  |\n217: | observability        | converging | 4                  |\n218: ```"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833527000,"end":1794833528229}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833528258,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e46a3294001K7dToKwovCp2ze","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","messageID":"msg_1e46a19a4001zyT0305VAt0Fr9","type":"tool","id":"call_972e72caaeb3446cb3bd3545","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"OUTPUT CONTRACT\" -A 40 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl | head -70"},"output":"106:  - the append gateway's own writes into the run directory when you invoke it (see OUTPUT CONTRACT item 2) — the gateway is the only writer of `{state_paths_state_log}`; that path is NEVER one you write directly\n107-- **BANNED OPERATIONS (NEVER execute against any path)**: `rm`, `rm -rf`, `git rm`, `mv`, `sed -i` (including `sed -i ''`), `rmdir`, `find ... -delete`, shell output-redirect truncate `>` against any file not in the allowed-write list, and any tool call whose effect is to delete, rename, or replace a file outside the allowed-write list. Reading is unrestricted; **writing, renaming, and deleting are scoped**.\n108-- **SCOPE VIOLATION PROTOCOL**: if your plan would require modifying any path NOT in the allowed-write list, you MUST STOP that action and emit a finding instead. Record the would-be mutation as a `scope_violation` entry in the iteration narrative (under a `## SCOPE VIOLATIONS` heading) and continue the review. NEVER execute the out-of-scope mutation. The review packet (`{state_paths_iteration_pattern}` directory and parents) is the only zone for your writes; the reviewed target spec/code is off-limits.\n109-- **GATEWAY CALLS ARE REQUIRED AND IN-SCOPE — NEVER A CONTAINMENT VIOLATION**: running `append-mode-event.cjs` against your own run directory is REQUIRED every iteration, not optional. Its writes land inside the run directory, which is your own write authority — that is never the \"out-of-scope write\" any containment warning means. \"Don't run the repo's tooling\" guidance targets builds, tests, and repo-wide scripts (e.g. `generate-context.js`, `validate.sh --recursive`, git writes); it does NOT exempt this state-recording gateway. Skipping the gateway call, or writing `{state_paths_state_log}` directly instead, fails the iteration.\n110-- Append JSONL record with dimensions, filesReviewed, findingsSummary, findingsNew, traceabilityChecks, newFindingsRatio, and optional graphEvents.\n111-- When emitting the iteration JSONL record, include an optional `graphEvents` array representing coverage graph nodes and edges discovered this iteration. Omit the field when no graph events are produced. Each event MUST use one of these two EXACT shapes. The reducer discriminates node vs edge by `type`, then validates each node's `kind` against the node vocabulary and each edge's `relation` against the relation vocabulary — any event outside these vocabularies is silently dropped, and if every event is dropped the convergence graph stays empty (nodeCount 0, empty signals):\n112-  - Node: `{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"<stable-id>\",\"kind\":\"<SLICE|DIMENSION|FILE|FINDING|EVIDENCE|REMEDIATION|BUG_CLASS|INVARIANT|PRODUCER|CONSUMER|TEST>\",\"label\":\"<short human name>\"}` — the semantic kind goes in the dedicated `kind` field (uppercase, one of those listed); `label` is a free-text display name ONLY, never the kind.\n113-  - Edge: `{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"<stable-id>\",\"source\":\"<nodeId>\",\"target\":\"<nodeId>\",\"relation\":\"<COVERS|EVIDENCE_FOR|CONTRADICTS|RESOLVES|CONFIRMS|ESCALATES|IN_DIMENSION|IN_FILE>\"}` — use `source`/`target`/`relation` (NOT `from`/`to`/`label`); `source` and `target` must reference node `id`s.\n114-\n115:## OUTPUT CONTRACT\n116-\n117-You MUST produce THREE artifacts per iteration. The YAML-owned post_dispatch_validate step emits a `schema_mismatch` conflict event if any is missing or malformed.\n118-\n119-1. **Iteration narrative markdown** at `{state_paths_iteration_pattern}` (path pre-substituted for the current iteration number). Structure: headings for Dimension, Files Reviewed, Findings by Severity (P0/P1/P2), Traceability Checks, Verdict, Next Dimension.\n120-\n121-2. **Canonical iteration record recorded THROUGH THE APPEND GATEWAY** — never written to `{state_paths_state_log}` directly — the gateway is its only writer, and it refreshes that log from the ledger after authorizing, fencing, and receipting the record. The record MUST use `\"type\":\"iteration\"` EXACTLY, NOT `\"iteration_delta\"` or any other variant. The reducer counts records where `type === \"iteration\"` only; other types are silently ignored. Required schema:\n122-\n123-```json\n124-{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":<n>,\"mode\":\"review\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-review\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review\",\"run\":\"<run-id>\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"<dimension-or-focus>\",\"dimensions\":[\"...\"],\"filesReviewed\":[\"path:line\"],\"findingsCount\":<n>,\"findingsSummary\":{\"P0\":<n>,\"P1\":<n>,\"P2\":<n>},\"findingsNew\":[],\"findingDetails\":[],\"traceabilityChecks\":{\"results\":[{\"protocolId\":\"spec_code\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\"path:line\"],\"summary\":\"<one line>\"}]},\"newFindingsRatio\":<0..1>,\"sessionId\":\"<session-id>\",\"generation\":<n>,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"timestamp\":\"<ISO-8601>\",\"durationMs\":<n>,\"graphEvents\":[/* optional */]}\n125-```\n126-\n127-### v2 Search Depth Output (when scopeClass is standard or complex)\n128-\n129-For standard or complex review scope, set `\"reviewDepthSchemaVersion\":2` on the same iteration JSONL record and include these v2 fields in addition to the v1 fields above:\n130-\n131-- `reviewDepthApplicability`: `{scopeClass,enforcement,reason,evidenceRefs}` where `scopeClass` is `trivial`, `standard`, or `complex`; `enforcement` is `strict`, `warn`, or `skip`.\n132-- `targetSelection`: `{selectedTargets,selectionReason,discoveryMethods,omittedHighRiskTargets,graphStatus,semanticSearchStatus,evidenceRefs}`. Name how targets were chosen, what high-risk targets were omitted, and whether graph/semantic search was available, unavailable, or partial.\n133-- `searchCoverage`: `{requiredBugClasses,covered,ruledOut,deferred,blocked,graphCoverageMode}` where `graphCoverageMode` is `graph`, `graphless_fallback`, or `unavailable_blocked`.\n134-- `searchLedger[]`: ledger rows with required `id`, `dimension`, `targetRefs`, `bugClass`, `disposition`, and `rationale`; include `hypothesis` or `invariant` (at least one); include `searchActions[]` with `{method,queryOrPath,result,evidenceRefs}`.\n135-- Each ledger row needs exactly one disposition link: `linkedFindingId` for `finding` (must match an id in `findingDetails[]`), `ruledOutReason` for `ruled_out`, `deferredReason` for `deferred`, `blockedReason` for `blocked`, or `notApplicableReason` for `not_applicable`.\n136-\n137-Trivial-scope exemption: when `scopeClass` is `trivial` and `enforcement` is `skip`, `searchLedger` may be `[]`, but `reviewDepthApplicability.evidenceRefs` MUST cite proof that the target is trivial.\n138-\n139-Compact v2 example:\n140-\n141-```json\n142-{\"reviewDepthSchemaVersion\":2,\"reviewDepthApplicability\":{\"scopeClass\":\"standard\",\"enforcement\":\"strict\",\"reason\":\"non-trivial target\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"path/to/file.ts:42\"]},\"targetSelection\":{\"selectedTargets\":[\"path/to/file.ts\"],\"selectionReason\":\"state transition producer\",\"discoveryMethods\":[\"direct_read\",\"exact_search\"],\"omittedHighRiskTargets\":[],\"graphStatus\":\"unavailable\",\"semanticSearchStatus\":\"partial\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"path/to/file.ts:42\"]},\"searchCoverage\":{\"requiredBugClasses\":[\"state_transition\"],\"covered\":[],\"ruledOut\":[\"state_transition\"],\"deferred\":[],\"blocked\":[],\"graphCoverageMode\":\"graphless_fallback\"},\"searchLedger\":[{\"id\":\"SL-001\",\"dimension\":\"correctness\",\"targetRefs\":[\"path/to/file.ts\"],\"bugClass\":\"state_transition\",\"hypothesis\":\"state transition can skip validation\",\"searchActions\":[{\"method\":\"direct_read\",\"queryOrPath\":\"path/to/file.ts\",\"result\":\"guard present on all branches\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"path/to/file.ts:42\"]}],\"disposition\":\"ruled_out\",\"rationale\":\"all branches call the guard\",\"ruledOutReason\":\"verified by direct read\"}]}\n143-```\n144-\n145-Legacy unversioned records remain valid during rollout. Phase D validator behavior should warn on legacy shallow records and strictly enforce this shape only for explicit v2 records.\n146-\n147-Record this single JSON object through the append gateway — do NOT `echo`/`>>` it into `{state_paths_state_log}` (the gateway is its only writer and refreshes it from the ledger). Write the one-line record to a temp file, then run:\n148-\n149-```bash\n150-node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs \\\n151-  --mode review \\\n152-  --run-directory \"$(dirname '{state_paths_state_log}')\" \\\n153-  --event-json <that temp file>\n154-```\n155-\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"106:  - the append gateway's own writes into the run directory when you invoke it (see OUTPUT CONTRACT item 2) — the gateway is the only writer of `{state_paths_state_log}`; that path is NEVER one you write directly\n107-- **BANNED OPERATIONS (NEVER execute against any path)**: `rm`, `rm -rf`, `git rm`, `mv`, `sed -i` (including `sed -i ''`), `rmdir`, `find ... -delete`, shell output-redirect truncate `>` against any file not in the allowed-write list, and any tool call whose effect is to delete, rename, or replace a file outside the allowed-write list. Reading is unrestricted; **writing, renaming, and deleting are scoped**.\n108-- **SCOPE VIOLATION PROTOCOL*