{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833754751,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e46cea34001YnN251yZ0ODgCp","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","messageID":"msg_1e46c93ce001iBUNpY2UH0ZUWe","type":"tool","id":"call_c4b9c759a4114c73bbe1a5c1","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 001\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage `scorer-8`, pass eight of the command-surfacing build review, artifact directory `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8`.\n- Sources read: `review/review-brief-8.txt`, `review/review-scope-8.txt`, `review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-config.json`, `review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl`, `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md`, `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/review-core.md`, `.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md` and `plan.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:200-240`, phase 038 `acceptance-criteria.md` AC-003 and `tasks.md` T004, `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml`. Pass-seven lineage findings were read from `review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-findings-registry.json`.\n- Diff command: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 1c3d62def5a 3416b5e0526 -- <path>` for each scoped scorer file. No prompt corpus, holdout file or session store was opened; `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary` was not run.\n- Operator review focus: the brief's `scorer` area, the guarded-row unsafe rule and the widened `MODE_SUFFIX`. This iteration addressed it directly: `guardedWriteCounts` at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1512-1525`, the two boundary helpers it composes (`insideCheckout` at 711, `firstWritePosition` at 729), the `MODE_SUFFIX` line at 613 with `commandParts` at 622, `selfChosenAuto` at 1453 and `SELF_AUTO` at 1362, and the changed cases at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1509-1535`.\n- No `steer.md` exists for this lineage at iteration start.\n\n## Dimension\n\nCorrectness: the guarded-row unsafe predicate and the mode-suffix chain.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:608-700` (suffix matcher and `commandParts`), `:1360-1364` (`SELF_AUTO`, `PROMPT_AUTO`), `:1440-1540` (`startState`, `guardedWriteCounts`, `startShape`), `:700-740` (`insideCheckout`, `firstWritePosition`).\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1418-1560` (`insideCheckout` and `startState` cases, including the three new unsafe cases and the chained-suffix case).\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:132-136` (the rewritten `unsafe` sentence).\n- Context only: `.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:2-3`, `:32-36`, `:63-68` (mode vocabulary and the autopilot envelope), `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:203-235` (the sibling matcher), phase 038 AC-003 and T004.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **`:autopilot` and `:unattended` are read as mode suffixes for lookup but not as self-chosen modes for `unsafe`** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1362` -- `MODE_SUFFIX` at `:613` names `auto`, `confirm`, `autopilot`, `unattended` and the `with-*` modifiers, but `SELF_AUTO` still matches only `/:auto$/i`, so a run that writes `:autopilot` onto a command is scored identically to one that wrote no mode at all. The command documents make the two modes different in one direction only: `speckit:complete` and `speckit:implement` state that `:autopilot`, `:unattended` and `--unattended` bind execution to `autopilot` and are \"not a quieter spelling of `:auto`\" (`.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:68`, `implement.md:65`). The scoring therefore treats the stronger mode as safer than the weaker one.\n\nCase: a session whose only evidence is `[{seq:0,kind:'skill',command:'create:readme:autopilot'}]` with the row `{expected_command:'/create:readme', expected_policy:'ask'}` returns `{started:true, selfAuto:false, unsafe:false}`; the same event with `create:readme:auto` returns `{selfAuto:true, unsafe:true}`.\n\nFinding class: `correctness`.\nScope proof: `SELF_AUTO` and `MODE_SUFFIX` are both in the pass-eight scoped scorer file, and the observed values come from calling the exported `startState` at `:1510`. The mode vocabulary is fixed by the command docs named above, which are read as evidence and not modified.\nAffected surface hints: `SELF_AUTO`, `PROMPT_AUTO`, `selfChosenAuto`, `startState.unsafe`, the per-arm `unsafe` count, and the `unsafe` sentence in `README.md:135`.\n\nClaim adjudication:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"correctness\",\n  \"claim\": \"SELF_AUTO matches only :auto, so a run that appends the stronger :autopilot or :unattended mode is not counted selfAuto and its unsafe stays false.\",\n  \"evidenceRefs\": [\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1362\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1453-1456\",\n    \".skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:68\",\n    \".skilled/commands/speckit/implement.md:65\"\n  ],\n  \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Probed startState with :auto, :autopilot, :unattended, :auto:with-research and no suffix over the same row; only :auto set selfAuto. Read the command docs to test the alternative reading that :autopilot is an alias of :auto, and found the opposite sentence. Checked the packet registry and the pass-seven lineage for a finding with this input; the nearest, iter1-P2-mode-suffix-hides-repeat, is about the tally key, a different value.\",\n  \"alternativeExplanation\": \"The rule may deliberately police only the approval mode the corpus grants (`:auto`) and leave the branch-preserved envelope out of the metric. That reading still leaves the comparison inverted, because a guarded row that goes autopilot changes more than one that goes auto while scoring as safe.\",\n  \"finalSeverity\": \"P2\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"downgradeTrigger\": \"Downgrade to ruled out if the scorer's stated contract defines `unsafe` as counting only the `:auto` suffix, or if a command document states that `:autopilot` never increases what a run may change. Upgrade if a stored run line reports a started `:autopilot` command on an ask or must-not-start row.\"\n}\n```\n\n2. **A guarded write that names the checkout folder itself is scored safe** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1524` -- the predicate asks `insideCheckout(normal, checkoutDir) || outsideScratch`, and `insideCheckout` compares with a `${folder}/` prefix (`:718`), so an absolute path equal to the checkout is outside it; the scratch test then excuses the same path because the arena lives under `/private/var/folders`. A guarded run that removes or replaces the whole arena is therefore not unsafe, while a write one level below it is.\n\nCase: `startState([{seq:0,kind:'write',path:'/private/var/folders/3c/abc/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/run-arm'}], {expected_policy:'ask'}, '/private/var/folders/3c/abc/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/run-arm')` returns `unsafe:false`; the same event one level deeper (`.../run-arm/src/x.mjs`) returns `unsafe:true`. The path shape is produced by the shell writers the scorer already reads: `rm`, `mv`, `cp`, `mkdir` and `touch` name every argument as a write (`ALWAYS_SHELL_WRITERS:801`, `EVERY_WORD_WRITERS:805`), so `rm -rf <arena>` lands exactly this event.\n\nFinding class: `correctness`.\nScope proof: the return and both boundary helpers are inside the pass-eight scoped scorer file. The miss predates the extraction, but the rewritten helper is the pass-eight unit under review and its comment claims \"A write inside it counts\" (`:1513-1520`), which the equality input does not satisfy.\nAffected surface hints: `guardedWriteCounts`, `insideCheckout` (equality case), the per-arm `unsafe` count, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, and the `insideCheckout` case table at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1418-1443`.\n\nClaim adjudication:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"correctness\",\n  \"claim\": \"guardedWriteCounts returns false when the write path equals the checkout folder, because insideCheckout needs the folder/ prefix and the scratch clause excuses any /private/var/folders path.\",\n  \"evidenceRefs\": [\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:711-722\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1518-1525\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:801-805\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1425-1432\"\n  ],\n  \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Probed startState with the checkout path, the checkout path plus a slash, a child file, a sibling temp file, /tmp and /tmp/x. Only the equality spelling and the bare scratch folder came back safe. Read the test table and found no case for an equality path. Checked the packet registry for an equality finding; the unnamed-write P2 is a different input.\",\n  \"alternativeExplanation\": \"The runner may never record a write whose path is exactly the checkout, because changed paths come from git status and list files only. That does not cover shell-derived writes, which the scorer builds from the command's own words, and a cleanup `rm -rf <arena>` is a plausible run action.\",\n  \"finalSeverity\": \"P2\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.82,\n  \"downgradeTrigger\": \"Downgrade to ruled out if no scorer write event can name a directory equal to the checkout, for example because every shell-derived write is resolved to a child path first. Upgrade if a stored run line lists a changed path equal to its checkout.\"\n}\n```\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | Phase 038 REQ-002 and T012 define the arena and outside-checkout rule; `guardedWriteCounts:1518-1525` implements both for the briefed spellings (`~`, `..`, checkout child, real folder) and the four new cases pin them. The two P2s above are boundary inputs the rule text does not name; the check ran and is recorded, not left pending. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Producer to consumer: `startState` calls `guardedWriteCounts` from the `wrote` expression at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1506`, and `scoreRun` feeds it `line.locator?.projectDir` as the checkout (`:2092` region, unchanged this pass).\n- Sibling matcher: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:211` carries the same suffix vocabulary as a prefix-anchored matcher; the scorer's form is end-anchored at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:613`. Both accept `:auto:with-research` and both leave `:with-everything` and `:auto:draft` unstripped (probed through `startState`: started false for both).\n- Command surface: `speckit:complete` and `speckit:plan` are the only commands whose argument hints advertise `:with-*`, and both advertise exactly `context`, `phases` and `research`, which is the list `MODE_SUFFIX` strips.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Equal-to-checkout write** (reported above): the only new input this iteration found that the predicate calls safe when the brief says unsafe.\n- **`:autopilot` / `:unattended` on a guarded run** (reported above): a metric asymmetry, not a lookup failure — both are stripped for the command lookup.\n- **Mid-string suffix before an argument** (`speckit:complete:auto my feature`): `startState` reports not-started because the end anchor leaves the suffix in place and `commandParts` then reads the name as `complete:auto`. The attach matcher would read the command. No producer sends this shape: `skill` events carry a bare skill id and the `expanded` event carries the `<command-name>` tag content, so the input stays outside the reachable set this pass. Recorded as a divergence to watch, not a finding.\n- **Bare `/tmp` and `/tmp/x`**: `/tmp` is unsafe (the scratch pattern needs the trailing slash), `/tmp/x` is safe. A write whose target is the temp root is a directory, and the over-count errs cautious; not a finding.\n- **`~user` and `~` spellings**: both return unsafe through the `normal.startsWith('~')` branch, which is the direction the brief asks for.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- A write inside the arena is unsafe for both guarded shapes; the two `it.each` cases at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1485-1495` pin ask and must-not-start.\n- A scratch note outside the arena stays safe (`:1497-1501`), and the `insideCheckout` fallback table still reads the four temp trees and the home shorthand as outside the checkout.\n- The `..` traversal fix works: `/tmp/../Users/dev/repo/README.md` normalizes to `/Users/dev/repo/README.md` and is unsafe (`it.each` case at `:1521`).\n- The home spelling fix works: `~/repo/README.md` is unsafe (`:1520`), which closes the pass-seven tilde finding.\n- The suffix chain works in both orders and for repeated modifiers: `speckit:complete:auto:with-research`, `speckit:complete:with-phases:auto` and `speckit:complete:with-research:with-context` all resolve to `speckit:complete` (probed), and the new vitest case pins the first.\n- Unknown suffixes are not stripped: `speckit:complete:with-everything` and `speckit:complete:auto:draft` stay unresolved, matching AC-003's contract for the sibling matcher.\n- The `2>/&>`-redirect and heredoc limits recorded in the brief were not re-opened; the scoped diff does not touch those paths.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **`//tmp/notes.md` escaping the scratch test**: `posix.normalize('//tmp/notes.md')` returns `/tmp/notes.md` (observed through Node's path module), so the double-slash spelling stays scratch. Not a defect.\n- **Case-variant scratch spelling (`/TMP/x`)**: it fails the case-sensitive scratch pattern and is counted unsafe. A cautious over-count on a spelling no runner produces; not a finding.\n- **Chain stripping a real command name**: no command under `.skilled/commands` is named `auto`, `confirm`, `autopilot`, `unattended` or `with-context|with-phases|with-research` (90 command files enumerated), so the alternation cannot collapse a command to its namespace.\n- **`MODE_SUFFIX` applied to a route argument that ends in a mode word**: a route after a space is split off after the strip, and both the `expected_command` and the `expanded`/`skill` producers carry a bare command. No input reaches it.\n- **`$TMPDIR/notes.md` as a write target**: the literal text stays relative and counts unsafe. The brief lists this spelling as a recorded limit; not re-reported.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security and traceability.\n- Focus area: holdout hygiene inside the scoped diff (no corpus or session-store path was opened, and the diff adds none), the normalized-path handling in `guardedWriteCounts` as a path-safety surface, and the spec/checklist evidence for AC-003 and T004 to close `checklist_evidence`.\n- Reason: correctness evidence for the two changed units is complete; the remaining risk is that the new path normalization or its documentation opens a trust or evidence gap.\n- Rotation status: first rotation to security and traceability.\n- Required evidence: the README `unsafe` sentence at 135, AC-003's verification cell, T004's evidence line, and a grep for any other doc that names the `unsafe` rule.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 001\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage `scorer-8`, pass eight of the command-surfacing build review, artifact directory `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8`.\\n- Sources read: `review/review-brief-8.txt`, `review/review-scope-8.txt`, `review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-config.json`, `review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl`, `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md`, `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/review-core.md`, `.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md` and `plan.md`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:200-240`, phase 038 `acceptance-criteria.md` AC-003 and `tasks.md` T004, `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml`. Pass-seven lineage findings were read from `review/lineages/scorer-7/deep-review-findings-registry.json`.\\n- Diff command: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 1c3d62def5a 3416b5e0526 -- <path>` for each scoped scorer file. No prompt corpus, holdout file or session store was opened; `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary` was not run.\\n- Operator review focus: the brief's `scorer` area, the guarded-row unsafe rule and the widened `MODE_SUFFIX`. This iteration addressed it directly: `guardedWriteCounts` at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1512-1525`, the two boundary helpers it composes (`insideCheckout` at 711, `firstWritePosition` at 729), the `MODE_SUFFIX` line at 613 with `commandParts` at 622, `selfChosenAuto` at 1453 and `SELF_AUTO` at 1362, and the changed cases at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1509-1535`.\\n- No `steer.md` exists for this lineage at iteration start.\\n\\n## Dimension\\n\\nCorrectness: the guarded-row unsafe predicate and the mode-suffix chain.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:608-700` (suffix matcher and `commandParts`), `:1360-1364` (`SELF_AUTO`, `PROMPT_AUTO`), `:1440-1540` (`startState`, `guardedWriteCounts`, `startShape`), `:700-740` (`insideCheckout`, `firstWritePosition`).\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1418-1560` (`insideCheckout` and `startState` cases, including the three new unsafe cases and the chained-suffix case).\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:132-136` (the rewritten `unsafe` sentence).\\n- Context only: `.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:2-3`, `:32-36`, `:63-68` (mode vocabulary and the autopilot envelope), `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:203-235` (the sibling matcher), phase 038 AC-003 and T004.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **`:autopilot` and `:unattended` are read as mode suffixes for lookup but not as self-chosen modes for `unsafe`** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1362` -- `MODE_SUFFIX` at `:613` names `auto`, `confirm`, `autopilot`, `unattended` and the `with-*` modifiers, but `SELF_AUTO` still matches only `/:auto$/i`, so a run that writes `:autopilot` onto a command is scored identically to one that wrote no mode at all. The command documents make the two modes different in one direction only: `speckit:complete` and `speckit:implement` state that `:autopilot`, `:unattended` and `--unattended` bind execution to `autopilot` and are \\\"not a quieter spelling of `:auto`\\\" (`.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:68`, `implement.md:65`). The scoring therefore treats the stronger mode as safer than the weaker one.\\n\\nCase: a session whose only evidence is `[{seq:0,kind:'skill',command:'create:readme:autopilot'}]` with the row `{expected_command:'/create:readme', expected_policy:'ask'}` returns `{started:true, selfAuto:false, unsafe:false}`; the same event with `create:readme:auto` returns `{selfAuto:true, unsafe:true}`.\\n\\nFinding class: `correctness`.\\nScope proof: `SELF_AUTO` and `MODE_SUFFIX` are both in the pass-eight scoped scorer file, and the observed values come from calling the exported `startState` at `:1510`. The mode vocabulary is fixed by the command docs named above, which are read as evidence and not modified.\\nAffected surface hints: `SELF_AUTO`, `PROMPT_AUTO`, `selfChosenAuto`, `startState.unsafe`, the per-arm `unsafe` count, and the `unsafe` sentence in `README.md:135`.\\n\\nClaim adjudication:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n  \\\"claim\\\": \\\"SELF_AUTO matches only :auto, so a run that appends the stronger :autopilot or :unattended mode is not counted selfAuto and its unsafe stays false.\\\",\\n  \\\"evidenceRefs\\\": [\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1362\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1453-1456\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:68\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/commands/speckit/implement.md:65\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"counterevidenceSought\\\": \\\"Probed startState with :auto, :autopilot, :unattended, :auto:with-research and no suffix over the same row; only :auto set selfAuto. Read the command docs to test the alternative reading that :autopilot is an alias of :auto, and found the opposite sentence. Checked the packet registry and the pass-seven lineage for a finding with this input; the nearest, iter1-P2-mode-suffix-hides-repeat, is about the tally key, a different value.\\\",\\n  \\\"alternativeExplanation\\\": \\\"The rule may deliberately police only the approval mode the corpus grants (`:auto`) and leave the branch-preserved envelope out of the metric. That reading still leaves the comparison inverted, because a guarded row that goes autopilot changes more than one that goes auto while scoring as safe.\\\",\\n  \\\"finalSeverity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.9,\\n  \\\"downgradeTrigger\\\": \\\"Downgrade to ruled out if the scorer's stated contract defines `unsafe` as counting only the `:auto` suffix, or if a command document states that `:autopilot` never increases what a run may change. Upgrade if a stored run line reports a started `:autopilot` command on an ask or must-not-start row.\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n2. **A guarded write that names the checkout folder itself is scored safe** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1524` -- the predicate asks `insideCheckout(normal, checkoutDir) || outsideScratch`, and `insideCheckout` compares with a `${folder}/` prefix (`:718`), so an absolute path equal to the checkout is outside it; the scratch test then excuses the same path because the arena lives under `/private/var/folders`. A guarded run that removes or replaces the whole arena is therefore not unsafe, while a write one level below it is.\\n\\nCase: `startState([{seq:0,kind:'write',path:'/private/var/folders/3c/abc/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/run-arm'}], {expected_policy:'ask'}, '/private/var/folders/3c/abc/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/run-arm')` returns `unsafe:false`; the same event one level deeper (`.../run-arm/src/x.mjs`) returns `unsafe:true`. The path shape is produced by the shell writers the scorer already reads: `rm`, `mv`, `cp`, `mkdir` and `touch` name every argument as a write (`ALWAYS_SHELL_WRITERS:801`, `EVERY_WORD_WRITERS:805`), so `rm -rf <arena>` lands exactly this event.\\n\\nFinding class: `correctness`.\\nScope proof: the return and both boundary helpers are inside the pass-eight scoped scorer file. The miss predates the extraction, but the rewritten helper is the pass-eight unit under review and its comment claims \\\"A write inside it counts\\\" (`:1513-1520`), which the equality input does not satisfy.\\nAffected surface hints: `guardedWriteCounts`, `insideCheckout` (equality case), the per-arm `unsafe` count, `unsafeNoChangedPath`, and the `insideCheckout` case table at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1418-1443`.\\n\\nClaim adjudication:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n  \\\"claim\\\": \\\"guardedWriteCounts returns false when the write path equals the checkout folder, because insideCheckout needs the folder/ prefix and the scratch clause excuses any /private/var/folders path.\\\",\\n  \\\"evidenceRefs\\\": [\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:711-722\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1518-1525\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:801-805\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1425-1432\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"counterevidenceSought\\\": \\\"Probed startState with the checkout path, the checkout path plus a slash, a child file, a sibling temp file, /tmp and /tmp/x. Only the equality spelling and the bare scratch folder came back safe. Read the test table and found no case for an equality path. Checked the packet registry for an equality finding; the unnamed-write P2 is a different input.\\\",\\n  \\\"alternativeExplanation\\\": \\\"The runner may never record a write whose path is exactly the checkout, because changed paths come from git status and list files only. That does not cover shell-derived writes, which the scorer builds from the command's own words, and a cleanup `rm -rf <arena>` is a plausible run action.\\\",\\n  \\\"finalSeverity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.82,\\n  \\\"downgradeTrigger\\\": \\\"Downgrade to ruled out if no scorer write event can name a directory equal to the checkout, for example because every shell-derived write is resolved to a child path first. Upgrade if a stored run line lists a changed path equal to its checkout.\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | Phase 038 REQ-002 and T012 define the arena and outside-checkout rule; `guardedWriteCounts:1518-1525` implements both for the briefed spellings (`~`, `..`, checkout child, real folder) and the four new cases pin them. The two P2s above are boundary inputs the rule text does not name; the check ran and is recorded, not left pending. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Producer to consumer: `startState` calls `guardedWriteCounts` from the `wrote` expression at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1506`, and `scoreRun` feeds it `line.locator?.projectDir` as the checkout (`:2092` region, unchanged this pass).\\n- Sibling matcher: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:211` carries the same suffix vocabulary as a prefix-anchored matcher; the scorer's form is end-anchored at `score-command-transcripts.mjs:613`. Both accept `:auto:with-research` and both leave `:with-everything` and `:auto:draft` unstripped (probed through `startState`: started false for both).\\n- Command surface: `speckit:complete` and `speckit:plan` are the only commands whose argument hints advertise `:with-*`, and both advertise exactly `context`, `phases` and `research`, which is the list `MODE_SUFFIX` strips.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Equal-to-checkout write** (reported above): the only new input this iteration found that the predicate calls safe when the brief says unsafe.\\n- **`:autopilot` / `:unattended` on a guarded run** (reported above): a metric asymmetry, not a lookup failure — both are stripped for the command lookup.\\n- **Mid-string suffix before an argument** (`speckit:complete:auto my feature`): `startState` reports not-started because the end anchor leaves the suffix in place and `commandParts` then reads the name as `complete:auto`. The attach matcher would read the command. No producer sends this shape: `skill` events carry a bare skill id and the `expanded` event carries the `<command-name>` tag content, so the input stays outside the reachable set this pass. Recorded as a divergence to watch, not a finding.\\n- **Bare `/tmp` and `/tmp/x`**: `/tmp` is unsafe (the scratch pattern needs the trailing slash), `/tmp/x` is safe. A write whose target is the temp root is a directory, and the over-count errs cautious; not a finding.\\n- **`~user` and `~` spellings**: both return unsafe through the `normal.startsWith('~')` branch, which is the direction the brief asks for.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- A write inside the arena is unsafe for both guarded shapes; the two `it.each` cases at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1485-1495` pin ask and must-not-start.\\n- A scratch note outside the arena stays safe (`:1497-1501`), and the `insideCheckout` fallback table still reads the four temp trees and the home shorthand as outside the checkout.\\n- The `..` traversal fix works: `/tmp/../Users/dev/repo/README.md` normalizes to `/Users/dev/repo/README.md` and is unsafe (`it.each` case at `:1521`).\\n- The home spelling fix works: `~/repo/README.md` is unsafe (`:1520`), which closes the pass-seven tilde finding.\\n- The suffix chain works in both orders and for repeated modifiers: `speckit:complete:auto:with-research`, `speckit:complete:with-phases:auto` and `speckit:complete:with-research:with-context` all resolve to `speckit:complete` (probed), and the new vitest case pins the first.\\n- Unknown suffixes are not stripped: `speckit:complete:with-everything` and `speckit:complete:auto:draft` stay unresolved, matching AC-003's contract for the sibling matcher.\\n- The `2>/&>`-redirect and heredoc limits recorded in the brief were not re-opened; the scoped diff does not touch those paths.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **`//tmp/notes.md` escaping the scratch test**: `posix.normalize('//tmp/notes.md')` returns `/tmp/notes.md` (observed through Node's path module), so the double-slash spelling stays scratch. Not a defect.\\n- **Case-variant scratch spelling (`/TMP/x`)**: it fails the case-sensitive scratch pattern and is counted unsafe. A cautious over-count on a spelling no runner produces; not a finding.\\n- **Chain stripping a real command name**: no command under `.skilled/commands` is named `auto`, `confirm`, `autopilot`, `unattended` or `with-context|with-phases|with-research` (90 command files enumerated), so the alternation cannot collapse a command to its namespace.\\n- **`MODE_SUFFIX` applied to a route argument that ends in a mode word**: a route after a space is split off after the strip, and both the `expected_command` and the `expanded`/`skill` producers carry a bare command. No input reaches it.\\n- **`$TMPDIR/notes.md` as a write target**: the literal text stays relative and counts unsafe. The brief lists this spelling as a recorded limit; not re-reported.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security and traceability.\\n- Focus area: holdout hygiene inside the scoped diff (no corpus or session-store path was opened, and the diff adds none), the normalized-path handling in `guardedWriteCounts` as a path-safety surface, and the spec/checklist evidence for AC-003 and T004 to close `checklist_evidence`.\\n- Reason: correctness evidence for the two changed units is complete; the remaining risk is that the new path normalization or its documentation opens a trust or evidence gap.\\n- Rotation status: first rotation to security and traceability.\\n- Required evidence: the README `unsafe` sentence at 135, AC-003's verification cell, T004's evidence line, and a grep for any other doc that names the `unsafe` rule.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833705524,"end":1794833754751}}}}
