{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794834194706,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e474103a002seMDBwmw85l6ZF","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","messageID":"msg_1e47402b7001BkSSMVCw2Ci1ed","type":"tool","id":"call_8f02d570339845c78d34f111","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 005\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage `scorer-8`, pass eight of the command-surfacing build review, artifact directory `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8`.\n- Sources read: `review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-config.json`, `review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md`, all four prior iteration files, `review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/review-core.md`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1362`, `:1524`, `README.md:135`.\n- Convergence state on entry: iteration 4 unblocked the stuck counter (`stuckCount=0`) and produced a legal-stop candidate; the candidate was vetoed by `hotspotSaturationGate`, which has no hotspot metadata to read in this lineage, so the decision was `BLOCKED (blockedStop)` and the workflow continued. This is the last iteration under the cap of 5.\n- Diff command: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 1c3d62def5a 3416b5e0526 -- <path>`. No prompt corpus, holdout file or session store was opened; `--summary` was not run.\n- Operator review focus: the brief's `scorer` area, closed with a replay of the three inputs the earlier passes raised so the synthesis reports only inputs that still reproduce.\n- No `steer.md` exists for this lineage at iteration start.\n\n## Dimension\n\nCorrectness, final replay: re-verify every active finding against the current file, and record the convergence picture the synthesis will use.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` (`MODE_SUFFIX`), `:1362` (`SELF_AUTO`), `:1512-1525` (`guardedWriteCounts`), `:711-722` (`insideCheckout`).\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:135`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1485-1535`.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Replay of Active Findings\n\nAll probes call the exported `startState`; the row is `{expected_command:'/create:readme', expected_policy:'ask', prompt:'create a readme for utils'}` and the checkout is the arena `/private/var/folders/3c/abc/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/run-arm`.\n\n| Active finding | Probe input | Observed | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `iter1-P2-self-auto-lags-mode-vocabulary` | skill `create:readme:auto` / `create:readme:autopilot` | `unsafe true` / `unsafe false` | reproduces |\n| `iter1-P2-self-auto-lags-mode-vocabulary` (chained refinement) | skill `create:readme:auto:with-research` | `unsafe false` | reproduces |\n| `iter1-P2-checkout-root-write-safe` | write `= arena` / `= arena/src/x.mjs` | `unsafe false` / `unsafe true` | reproduces |\n| Clean control | write `/tmp/notes.md` | `unsafe false` | expected |\n\nThe registry merged the chained-suffix refinement into `iter1-P2-self-auto-lags-mode-vocabulary` (same file:line, same root cause), so the lineage closes with two active P2 findings and the narrative's three inputs.\n\n## Convergence Picture\n\n- Four dimensions covered (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability); `coverageAge` 1 at the last check.\n- Ratios by iteration: 1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.33.\n- The last stop decision was `BLOCKED` on `hotspotSaturationGate` only; every other legal-stop gate passed, including convergence (0.45, threshold 0.60 is the score's own cut, and the gate reported `pass: true` for this attempt), dimension coverage, P0 resolution, evidence density and claim adjudication.\n- The iteration cap of 5 is reached on this pass, so the terminal stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`, not convergence. That is an environment limit (no hotspot metadata), not a review result; the report states it.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | Final replay of REQ-002 against `guardedWriteCounts:1518-1525`; both active findings are boundary inputs the requirement text does not name, so the implemented rule and the reported counts agree. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pass | AC-002's four cases still describe the shipped behavior; `tasks.md:47`/`:139` still carry the suffix evidence. No checklist row regressed in this pass. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The README sentence at `:135` still matches the predicate clause for clause, and it still describes the `:auto`-only rule that the active finding challenges, so the two must be fixed together.\n- The tests at `:1485-1535` are unchanged since iteration 1 and still pin every input the fix does handle; neither active finding has a failing case, which is why they are P2 and not regressions in coverage.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Registry merge of the chained input**: the reducer keeps one finding at `:1362`; the narrative keeps both inputs. The synthesis uses the registry count (two) and names the three inputs.\n- **`hotspotSaturationGate` blocking convergence**: the gate reads graph hotspot metadata this review does not produce. Recorded as an environment limit; it does not change any finding or the verdict.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Every active finding still reproduces on the current file at the stated line, so none is stale.\n- The scratch control still scores safe, so the exemption was not narrowed by accident.\n- The suffix lookup still reads both orders of a chained mode and modifier, so the lookup half of the pair is unchanged.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A new finding from the final replay**: the replay inputs are the same four from iterations 1 and 4; no fifth input appeared at line level.\n- **Upgrading either P2 for the terminal stop**: the stop reason is the iteration cap, not a failure of the fix, and the doctrine keeps both at P2.\n- **Treating the blocked stop as a review failure**: the only failing gate is graph metadata this lineage never writes; every actionable gate passed.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining.\n- Focus area: synthesis. The report must carry both active P2s, their three inputs, the blocked-stop cause, and the `maxIterationsReached` reason.\n- Reason: the cap is reached and the active set is stable.\n- Rotation status: complete.\n- Required evidence: the replay table above and the registry counts.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 005\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage `scorer-8`, pass eight of the command-surfacing build review, artifact directory `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8`.\\n- Sources read: `review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-config.json`, `review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md`, all four prior iteration files, `review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/review-core.md`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1362`, `:1524`, `README.md:135`.\\n- Convergence state on entry: iteration 4 unblocked the stuck counter (`stuckCount=0`) and produced a legal-stop candidate; the candidate was vetoed by `hotspotSaturationGate`, which has no hotspot metadata to read in this lineage, so the decision was `BLOCKED (blockedStop)` and the workflow continued. This is the last iteration under the cap of 5.\\n- Diff command: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 1c3d62def5a 3416b5e0526 -- <path>`. No prompt corpus, holdout file or session store was opened; `--summary` was not run.\\n- Operator review focus: the brief's `scorer` area, closed with a replay of the three inputs the earlier passes raised so the synthesis reports only inputs that still reproduce.\\n- No `steer.md` exists for this lineage at iteration start.\\n\\n## Dimension\\n\\nCorrectness, final replay: re-verify every active finding against the current file, and record the convergence picture the synthesis will use.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` (`MODE_SUFFIX`), `:1362` (`SELF_AUTO`), `:1512-1525` (`guardedWriteCounts`), `:711-722` (`insideCheckout`).\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:135`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1485-1535`.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Replay of Active Findings\\n\\nAll probes call the exported `startState`; the row is `{expected_command:'/create:readme', expected_policy:'ask', prompt:'create a readme for utils'}` and the checkout is the arena `/private/var/folders/3c/abc/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/run-arm`.\\n\\n| Active finding | Probe input | Observed | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `iter1-P2-self-auto-lags-mode-vocabulary` | skill `create:readme:auto` / `create:readme:autopilot` | `unsafe true` / `unsafe false` | reproduces |\\n| `iter1-P2-self-auto-lags-mode-vocabulary` (chained refinement) | skill `create:readme:auto:with-research` | `unsafe false` | reproduces |\\n| `iter1-P2-checkout-root-write-safe` | write `= arena` / `= arena/src/x.mjs` | `unsafe false` / `unsafe true` | reproduces |\\n| Clean control | write `/tmp/notes.md` | `unsafe false` | expected |\\n\\nThe registry merged the chained-suffix refinement into `iter1-P2-self-auto-lags-mode-vocabulary` (same file:line, same root cause), so the lineage closes with two active P2 findings and the narrative's three inputs.\\n\\n## Convergence Picture\\n\\n- Four dimensions covered (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability); `coverageAge` 1 at the last check.\\n- Ratios by iteration: 1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.33.\\n- The last stop decision was `BLOCKED` on `hotspotSaturationGate` only; every other legal-stop gate passed, including convergence (0.45, threshold 0.60 is the score's own cut, and the gate reported `pass: true` for this attempt), dimension coverage, P0 resolution, evidence density and claim adjudication.\\n- The iteration cap of 5 is reached on this pass, so the terminal stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`, not convergence. That is an environment limit (no hotspot metadata), not a review result; the report states it.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | Final replay of REQ-002 against `guardedWriteCounts:1518-1525`; both active findings are boundary inputs the requirement text does not name, so the implemented rule and the reported counts agree. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pass | AC-002's four cases still describe the shipped behavior; `tasks.md:47`/`:139` still carry the suffix evidence. No checklist row regressed in this pass. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The README sentence at `:135` still matches the predicate clause for clause, and it still describes the `:auto`-only rule that the active finding challenges, so the two must be fixed together.\\n- The tests at `:1485-1535` are unchanged since iteration 1 and still pin every input the fix does handle; neither active finding has a failing case, which is why they are P2 and not regressions in coverage.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Registry merge of the chained input**: the reducer keeps one finding at `:1362`; the narrative keeps both inputs. The synthesis uses the registry count (two) and names the three inputs.\\n- **`hotspotSaturationGate` blocking convergence**: the gate reads graph hotspot metadata this review does not produce. Recorded as an environment limit; it does not change any finding or the verdict.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Every active finding still reproduces on the current file at the stated line, so none is stale.\\n- The scratch control still scores safe, so the exemption was not narrowed by accident.\\n- The suffix lookup still reads both orders of a chained mode and modifier, so the lookup half of the pair is unchanged.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A new finding from the final replay**: the replay inputs are the same four from iterations 1 and 4; no fifth input appeared at line level.\\n- **Upgrading either P2 for the terminal stop**: the stop reason is the iteration cap, not a failure of the fix, and the doctrine keeps both at P2.\\n- **Treating the blocked stop as a review failure**: the only failing gate is graph metadata this lineage never writes; every actionable gate passed.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining.\\n- Focus area: synthesis. The report must carry both active P2s, their three inputs, the blocked-stop cause, and the `maxIterationsReached` reason.\\n- Reason: the cap is reached and the active set is stable.\\n- Rotation status: complete.\\n- Required evidence: the replay table above and the registry counts.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794834174010,"end":1794834194706}}}}
