{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794834417064,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","part":{"partID":"prt_1e477ae20001Qoc6KGnbqv6Bsd","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c06ffemmJMnzkzBHTwnQ","messageID":"msg_1e477a03c001ViVnRxp03sYewq","type":"tool","id":"call_7f2fe0dd07bf439cba94562b","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Direct `startState` probes through the exported entry point turned each boundary question into an observed value, so every finding in this lineage carries a reproduced input rather than a reading of the code (iterations 1, 4, 5).\n- Diffing the scoped files against the pass-seven commit and reading the whole predicate (`guardedWriteCounts`, `insideCheckout`, `firstWritePosition`) exposed the equality gap that a hunk-only read would have missed (iteration 1).\n- Reading the command documents' argument hints settled the mode vocabulary question with a citation instead of a guess, and showed `:autopilot` is a stronger mode, not an alias (iterations 1, 4).\n- Replaying the active findings at the cap kept the registry honest: all three inputs still reproduce on the shipped lines (iteration 5).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Treating `:unattended`, `:with-research` and `:auto:with-research` as a purely mechanical suffix widening missed that the self-chosen-mode rule reads the same vocabulary; the asymmetry only appeared at line level in the recovery pass (iteration 4).\n- Two no-progress iterations in a row tripped `STUCK_RECOVERY`, which is why the lineage needed a recovery pass and the severity re-examination before it could stabilize (iteration 3).\n- A legal convergence stop was unavailable: `hotspotSaturationGate` has no hotspot metadata to read in a lineage, so the candidate was vetoed and the run ended at the iteration cap (iteration 5).\n","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1]\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1]\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -55,13 +55,18 @@\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1]\n+- Direct `startState` probes through the exported entry point turned each boundary question into an observed value, so every finding in this lineage carries a reproduced input rather than a reading of the code (iterations 1, 4, 5).\n+- Diffing the scoped files against the pass-seven commit and reading the whole predicate (`guardedWriteCounts`, `insideCheckout`, `firstWritePosition`) exposed the equality gap that a hunk-only read would have missed (iteration 1).\n+- Reading the command documents' argument hints settled the mode vocabulary question with a citation instead of a guess, and showed `:autopilot` is a stronger mode, not an alias (iterations 1, 4).\n+- Replaying the active findings at the cap kept the registry honest: all three inputs still reproduce on the shipped lines (iteration 5).\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1]\n+- Treating `:unattended`, `:with-research` and `:auto:with-research` as a purely mechanical suffix widening missed that the self-chosen-mode rule reads the same vocabulary; the asymmetry only appeared at line level in the recovery pass (iteration 4).\n+- Two no-progress iterations in a row tripped `STUCK_RECOVERY`, which is why the lineage needed a recovery pass and the severity re-examination before it could stabilize (iteration 3).\n+- A legal convergence stop was unavailable: `hotspotSaturationGate` has no hotspot metadata to read in a lineage, so the candidate was vetoed and the run ended at the iteration cap (iteration 5).\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n ### **`//tmp/notes.md` escaping the scratch test**: `posix.normalize('//tmp/notes.md')` returns `/tmp/notes.md` (observed through Node's path module), so the double-slash spelling stays scratch. Not a defect. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n","status":"modified","additions":7,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Direct `startState` probes through the exported entry point turned each boundary question into an observed value, so every finding in this lineage carries a reproduced input rather than a reading of the code (iterations 1, 4, 5).\\n- Diffing the scoped files against the pass-seven commit and reading the whole predicate (`guardedWriteCounts`, `insideCheckout`, `firstWritePosition`) exposed the equality gap that a hunk-only read would have missed (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the command documents' argument hints settled the mode vocabulary question with a citation instead of a guess, and showed `:autopilot` is a stronger mode, not an alias (iterations 1, 4).\\n- Replaying the active findings at the cap kept the registry honest: all three inputs still reproduce on the shipped lines (iteration 5).\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Treating `:unattended`, `:with-research` and `:auto:with-research` as a purely mechanical suffix widening missed that the self-chosen-mode rule reads the same vocabulary; the asymmetry only appeared at line level in the recovery pass (iteration 4).\\n- Two no-progress iterations in a row tripped `STUCK_RECOVERY`, which is why the lineage needed a recovery pass and the severity re-examination before it could stabilize (iteration 3).\\n- A legal convergence stop was unavailable: `hotspotSaturationGate` has no hotspot metadata to read in a lineage, so the candidate was vetoed and the run ended at the iteration cap (iteration 5).\\n\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1]\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1]\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-8/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794834411040,"end":1794834417064}}}}
